        "solution": "$2\\left(\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + i\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = 2\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2} + i\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = 1 + i\\sqrt{3}$.",
        "hint": "$\\cos\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$ et $\\sin\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."
      }
